From: "Caleb J. Westfall" <calebwestfall1989@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 14:11:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] SOTA-3: CJCS certified non-equivalence (experimental),
 ancestry-based CPU budget, timeout diagnosis

- proofscope/experimental/cjcs.py: Certified Joint-drift Countermodel Search. Self-extraction of each side
  (frozen extractor, one Lean process), refute-first countermodel search, proof of only the unrefuted side,
  kernel-checked certificates (frozen certify gate) of: logical difference (refutation + proof),
  logical equivalence (Iff.rfl, both false, both true), and drift-region explanations. Search failure is
  ABSTAIN. Frozen v1.2 untouched.
- research/cjcs/CJCS.lean: 15 theorems (9 axiom-free, 5 classical, 1 propext+Quot.sound): cjcs_sound,
  difference_needs_a_proof (a difference certificate contains a proof of one side), nonequiv_iff,
  disagreement_partition + regions_disjoint (complete, non-overlapping explanation),
  joint_failure_iff + joint_disjoint_harmless (individually harmless changes fail jointly exactly on the
  joint region).
- bench/limits.py: process tree by ancestry (pid, starttime) instead of session. Root cause of the BEq+
  3.654 s overshoot: LeanInteract starts its REPL with start_new_session=True, so it escaped the
  session-based limiter (reproduced: SOTA-2 limiter overshoot 1.019 s on a 1 s budget; now <= 0.09 s).
  Records polls and mean poll cost; runner records enforcement_ok against a 0.5 s tolerance.
- bench/diagnose.py: stage-level trace of v1.2 / CJCS (Lean process count, CPU per stage, import baseline).
- runner/adapters/outcomes/gate: 'cjcs' system (experimental, reported, not gated).
- bench/dev_sota3: 24 Mathlib development pairs with PROVISIONAL developer labels (+3 fixtures).
- .github/workflows/sota3-research.yml: theory + core suites, Mathlib diagnosis, 4-system development
  comparison at 20 CPU-s, provisional dev scoring. Push-triggered on research/sota3-cjcs.
- Local (core Lean): CJCS core dev 10/10 (tuned), held-out 11/14 on first run (hash recorded before),
  0 must-not-be violations; 31 unit tests pass. Mathlib results PENDING.

